Balls, which are approved for play under the
Rules of Tennis, must comply with the
specifications in Appendix I.
The International Tennis Federation shall rule on
the question of whether any ball or prototype
complies with Appendix I or is otherwise
approved, or not approved, for play. Such ruling
may be taken on its own initiative or upon
application by any party with a bona fide interest
therein, including any player, equipment
manufacturer or National Association or
members thereof. Such rulings and applications
shall be made in accordance with the applicable
Review and Hearing Procedures of the
International Tennis Federation (see AppendixXII.
