Notes:
1 This ball type may be pressurised or pressureless. The pressureless ball shall have an internal pressure that is
no greater than 7 kPa (1 psi) and may be used for high altitude play above 1,219 m (4,000 feet) above sea level
and shall have been acclimatised for 60 days or more at the altitude of the specific tournament.
2 This ball type is also recommended for high altitude play on any court surface type above 1,219 m (4,000 feet)
above sea level.
3 This ball type is pressurised and is specified for high altitude play above 1,219 m (4,000 feet) above sea level
only.
4 The deformation shall be the average of a single reading along each of three perpendicular axes. No two
individual readings shall differ by more than 0.08 cm (0.031 inches).
c.
